-- Reshape with a free axis (ex24, second program point): to 4 _ infers 64/4 = 16 columns. Twin of 050-reshape-positions.bqn (statements 1-2; program prefix extends 050-reshape-positions-a).
-- `_` is the free axis: give the pour every extent but one and it computes the missing one from the selection's count — 64 soldiers into 4 rows is 16 columns, no arithmetic in the source. The same muster re-formed wider.
-- This file also pins prefix extension: a longer prefix of the same program lands on the .bqn's intermediate state.
-- Same world: 70 entities, 64 soldiers, civs at keys 5 17 29 41 53 65. The second pour overwrites the first under the same full selection, so the final state equals the .bqn's pos2 computed from the sentinel pre-state.
-- Soldiers receive the row-major cells ⟨k div 16, k mod 16⟩ of the 4x16 lattice in key order; hand spot: key 20 is soldier ordinal 18 = 16+2 -> cell ⟨1,2⟩; bystanders keep ⟨-1,-1⟩.
--! registry ../registries/050-reshape-positions-a.reg
--! expect-n 70
--! expect pos = 0 0 0 1 0 2 0 3 0 4 -1 -1 0 5 0 6 0 7 0 8 0 9 0 10 0 11 0 12 0 13 0 14 0 15 -1 -1 1 0 1 1 1 2 1 3 1 4 1 5 1 6 1 7 1 8 1 9 1 10 -1 -1 1 11 1 12 1 13 1 14 1 15 2 0 2 1 2 2 2 3 2 4 2 5 -1 -1 2 6 2 7 2 8 2 9 2 10 2 11 2 12 2 13 2 14 2 15 3 0 -1 -1 3 1 3 2 3 3 3 4 3 5 3 6 3 7 3 8 3 9 3 10 3 11 -1 -1 3 12 3 13 3 14 3 15

Soldier , pos = to 8 8
Soldier , pos = to 4 _
